invariant: INV-35
file: build.h
catches: test/lib-check-webpki-record.sh
reason: CH_BUILD_AXES leaves out the CH_TRANSPORT_RECORD term. The object
  and every consumer compute the axes from the same header, so the two
  still agree and a comparison between them cannot see it: a
  record-mode object and a TLS one now differ in no bit. test/build_test.c
  restates the axes from its own defines, one line per define, and exits
  2 when CH_BUILD_AXES disagrees with them, so lib-check objects.

--- old
     CH_BUILD_IF_KEX_PQ | CH_BUILD_IF_TRANSPORT_QUIC | CH_BUILD_IF_TRANSPORT_RECORD |              \
--- new
     CH_BUILD_IF_KEX_PQ | CH_BUILD_IF_TRANSPORT_QUIC |                                             \
